2 CONT '''Eumenes''' (/juːˈmɛniːz/; Greek: Εὐμένης; fl. 362–315 BC) was a Greek general and satrap. He participated in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_Alexander_the_Great Wars of Alexander the Great], serving as both [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Alexander-the-Great-king-of-Macedonia/6000000007875679261 '''Alexander''']'s personal secretary and as a battlefield commander. He later was a participant in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_the_Diado
2 CONC chi Wars of the Diadochi] as a supporter of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonia_(ancient_kingdom)_ Macedonian] [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argead_dynasty Argead] royal house. He was executed after the [https://en.wikip
2 CONC edia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Gabiene Battle of Gabiene] in the winter of 316–315 BC. 
