2 CONT =Philotera=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Philotera (Greek: Φιλωτέρα, born 315/309 BC-probably after 282 BC and before 268 BC) was a Greek Macedonian noblewoman and a Greek Egyptian princess of the Ptolemaic dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philotera was the daughter of Ptolemy I Soter and Berenice I of Egypt. She had one older sister, Arsinoe II, and a younger brother, the future Pharaoh Ptolemy II Philadelphus. From her parents' previous marriages, Philotera had va
2 CONC rious half-maternal and half-paternal siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known of her life. Philotera died sometime before the accession of Ptolemy II to the Ptolemaic throne and before Arsinoe II died. The fact that Philotera died before her sister did is demonstrated by a hymn written by Ca
2 CONC llimachus on the death of Arsinoe II.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Philotera died, Ptolemy II deified her as a goddess. Ptolemy II erected a temple in her honor in Alexandria. Greeks and Egyptians worshiped her along with Arsinoe II, and Ptolemy II created a religious cult in her honor. Pto
2 CONC lemy II also founded a port town in the Red Sea called Philotera, which is modern Safaga.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philotera
