2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras En], [https://sh.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirhas Sh], [https://bs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirhas Bs]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' (king? *) - Greek sources do not provide and not mentioned information that he was a king, but it can be assumed that he was been a king. His surname isn't van  Elymiotis,  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sirras''' or '''Sirrhas''' (Ancient Greek: Σίρρας; d. 390 BC) was the son-in-law of the king of Lynkestis, Arrhabaeus (fl. 423–393 BC), having married his daughter Irra. He participated in an Illyrian-Lynkestian coalition's def
2 CONC eat of the attempted invasion of Lynkestis by the Macedonian king Archelaus. He may have been a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynkestis Lynkestian] [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_regent prince-regent] [1] or an [https://en
2 CONC .wikipedia.org/wiki/Illyrians Illyrian] chieftain, [2] part of the Illyrian force in a previous and also successful Illyrian-Lynkestian coalition against Sparta and Macedon during the Peloponnesian War. [3][4][5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sirras' daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Eurydice-queen-consort-of-Macedonia/6000000002188198835 '''Eurydice'''] married [https://www.geni.com/people/Amyntas-III-king-of-Macedonia/6000000006500864007 '''Amyntas III'''], king 
2 CONC of Macedon; the youngest of their sons was [https://www.geni.com/people/Phillip-II-The-One-Eye-king-of-Macedonia/6000000008248160118 '''Philip II of Macedon'''], father of [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-the-Great-king-of-M
2 CONC acedonia/6000000007875679261 '''Alexander the Great''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#Name Name Sirras]====
2 CONT
2 CONT The origin of the name Sirras or Sirrhas is somewhat obscure.[7][8] It has been suggested that the characteristic doubling of the r ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_alphabet Greek]: ρ) and the ending in -as (-ας) are typical 
2 CONC of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Macedonian_language Macedonian] names. [8][9] Historian [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldemar_Heckel Waldemar Hecke]l notes that the "name does not appear elsewhere in Upper Makedonia, n
2 CONC or does it repeat within the family",[8] but others interpret the name as being [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynkestis Lynkestian] and not attested in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illyria Illyria]. [10][11]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#Biography Biography]===
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#Origin Origin]====
2 CONT
2 CONT Sirras' origin is '''disputed''', scholars being mainly divided on whether he was [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illyrians Illyrian] [12] or [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynkestis Lynkestian]. [13] Some have theorized that his f
2 CONC ather was probably the Illyrian chieftain [https://www.geni.com/people/Grabos-I/6000000205380658823 '''Grabos'''], [14] while his mother was perhaps a native Macedonian.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT The only evidence for Sirras' ethnicity in ancient literature is the description of his daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Eurydice-queen-consort-of-Macedonia/6000000002188198835 Eurydice's] ethnicity, expressly described as "I
2 CONC llyrian", and through her maternal grand-father Arrhabaeus as "Lynkestian" from the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorians Doric Greek] [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bacchiadae Bacchiadae] family. Modern scholars are divided on w
2 CONC hether they are historically accurate or not, or whether they are mutually exclusive or not. [15][16]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#Participation_in_the_Peloponnesian_War Participation in the Peloponnesian War]====
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lyncestis Battle of Lyncestis]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#War_against_Archelaus_I_of_Macedon War against Archelaus I of Macedon]====
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#Family Family]====
2 CONT
2 CONT Sirras' daughter, [https://www.geni.com/people/Eurydice-queen-consort-of-Macedonia/6000000002188198835 '''Eurydice'''], married King [https://www.geni.com/people/Amyntas-III-king-of-Macedonia/6000000006500864007 '''Amyntas III''']
2 CONC  of Macedon in around 390 BC, probably in a Macedonian effort to establish an alliance with both the [https://www.geni.com/projects/Illyrians/4499239 '''Illyrians'''] and Lynkestians,[28] or to detach the Lynkestians from their hi
2 CONC storical alliance with the Illyrians,[24][29][30] after Amyntas was defeated by Illyrians or an Illyrian-Lynkestian coalition in 393 BC.[31][32] One of the sons from this marriage was the future [https://www.geni.com/people/Philli
2 CONC p-II-The-One-Eye-king-of-Macedonia/6000000008248160118 '''Philip II of Macedon''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirras#References References]====
2 CONT
