1 NOTE Ptolemy III (282?-221 bc), called Ptolemy Euergetes ("benefactor"), king 
2 CONT of Egypt (246-221 bc), the son of Ptolemy II. He reunited Cyrenaica and 
2 CONT Egypt, invaded the Seleucid Kingdom of Syria to avenge the murder of his 
2 CONT sister and her infant son, the heir to the Seleucid throne, and 
2 CONT established Egyptian naval predominance in the Aegean Sea. Ptolemy III was 
2 CONT a liberal patron of the arts and added to the collection of the 
2 CONT Alexandrian library. His rule marked the height of Egyptian power, 
2 CONT prosperity, and wealth under the Ptolemies.
