2 CONT =Bircenna=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bircenna (Ancient Greek: Βιρκέννα; ruled c. 292-272 BC) was an Illyrian princess and later an Epirote queen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bircenna was the daughter of Bardylis II of the Dardanian Kingdom. Bircenna was one of the five wives of Pyrrhus of Epirus; she married him around 292 BC. Pyrrhus married Bircenna for diplomatic reasons and to increase his power i
2 CONC n southern Illyria as he was an ally of Bircenna's father. Bircenna had a son named Helenus, who at an early age accompanied his father in his ambitious campaigns conducted in the Italian peninsula. Lanassa, one of the wives of Py
2 CONC rrhus, left him because she claimed that he took better care of his 'barbarian' wives.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bircenna
