1 NOTE Ptolemy V (210?-181 bc), called Ptolemy Epiphanes ("illustrious"), king of 
2 CONT Egypt (205-181 bc), grandson of Ptolemy II Euergetes. At the beginning of 
2 CONT his reign, Antiochus III of Syria and Philip V of Macedonia agreed to 
2 CONT divide the foreign possessions of Egypt between them, and Egypt was 
2 CONT greatly weakened. The official coronation of Ptolemy V was held in 197 bc; 
2 CONT it was the occasion on which the Egyptian priesthood published the decree 
2 CONT that forms the trilingual inscription on the Rosetta Stone. In 193 bc 
2 CONT Ptolemy married the Seleucid princess Cleopatra I.
