1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemy_X_Alexander_I
2 CONT
2 CONT Ptolemy X Alexander I (Greek: Πτολεμαῖος Ἀλέξανδρος, Ptolemaĩos Aléxandros) was King of Egypt from 110 BC to 109 BC and 107 BC till 88 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Ptolemy VIII Physcon and Cleopatra III. In 110 BC he became King with his mother as co-regent, after his mother had deposed his brother Ptolemy IX Lathyros. However, in 109 BC he was deposed by Ptolemy IX. In 107
2 CONC  BC he became King again, and again with his mother as co-regent. In 101 BC he had his mother killed, and ruled either alone or with his niece/wife, Berenice III.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he died, Ptolemy IX regained the throne. When Ptolemy IX died, Ptolemy X's wife Berenice III took over the throne for six months. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ptolomeo X . n. en 110 AC.  al 88 ac.Se convirtió de nuevo en rey, gobernando con su madre. Luego la depuso y la asesino. Casó Cleopatra Selene I y posteriormente  con Berenice III. Hizo varias  obras  públicas en  reparaciones de
2 CONC   Templos, sin  embargo hizo  un negocio ruinoso con Roma.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Ptolemy X Alexander I=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ptolemy X Alexander I (Greek: Πτολεμαῖος Ἀλέξανδρος, Ptolemaĩos Aléxandros) was King of Egypt from 110 BC to 109 BC and 107 BC till 88 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Ptolemy VIII Physcon and Cleopatra III. In 110 BC he became King with his mother as co-regent, after his mother had deposed his brother Ptolemy IX Lathyros. However, in 109 BC he was deposed by Ptolemy IX. In 107
2 CONC  BC he became King again, and again with his mother as co-regent. In 101 BC he had his mother killed, and ruled either alone or with his niece/wife, Berenice III.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he died, Ptolemy IX regained the throne. When Ptolemy IX died, Ptolemy X's wife Berenice III took over the throne for six months.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemy_X_Alexander_I
