1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Shalishuka=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Shalishuka (IAST: Śāliśuka) Maurya was a ruler of the Indian Maurya dynasty. He ruled from 215-202 BC. He was the successor of Samprati Maurya. While Yuga Purana section of the Gargi Samhita mentions him as quarrelsome, unrighteou
2 CONC s ruler, he is also called as being of "righteous words" but "unrighteous conduct" due to his patronage of Jainism. According to the Puranas he was succeeded by Devavarman.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shalishuka
