2 CONT =Diodotus II=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Diodotus II (Greek: Διόδοτος Β΄; c. 252 BC-c. 223 BC) was a Greco-Bactrian king from c. 239 BC, son of Diodotus I. He is known for concluding a peace treaty with the Parthian king Arsaces, in order to forestall the Seleucid reconq
2 CONC uest of both Parthia and Bactria:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''"Soon after, relieved by the death of Diodotus I, Arsaces made peace and concluded an alliance with his son, also by the name of Diodotus; some time later he fought against Seleucos who came to punish the rebels, but he prevaile
2 CONC d: the Parthians celebrated this day as the one that marked the beginning of their freedom" (Justin, XLI,4)''
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 230 or 223 BC, Diodotus was killed by an usurper, his brother-in-law Euthydemus I, founder of the Greco-Bactrian Euthydemid dynasty (Polybius, 11.34, 2).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diodotus_II
