1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''She is variously said to have been either a Syrian Greek freedwoman or a member of the royal family at Emesa.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Julia Urania
2 CONT * Born: flourished 1st century
2 CONT * Title: Queen of Mauretania
2 CONT * Spouse: Ptolemy of Mauretania
2 CONT * Children: Princess Drusilla
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Urania (Greek: Ιουλìα Ουρανìа, Latin: Ivlia Urania[1], flourished 1st century) was a Roman Client Queen of Mauretania. She married the Roman Client King Ptolemy of Mauretania, who was a son of the former Mauretanian Client M
2 CONC onarchs Juba II and Cleopatra Selene II.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania became Queen of Mauretania, through her marriage to Ptolemy. She married Ptolemy at an unknown date in the 1st century and had borne Ptolemy, a daughter called Drusilla who was born in 38.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania is only known through a funeral inscription of her Freedwoman Julia Bodina found at Cherchell, Algeria.[4] Cherchell was then known as Caesaria, the capital of the Roman Client Kingdom of Mauretania in the Roman Empire. In 
2 CONC Bodina’s funeral inscription, Bodina ascribes Urania as Queen Julia Urania. She was ascribed as Queen as a local courtesy or probably a posthumus honor as a dedication to the memory of the former ruling monarch. The inscription re
2 CONC veals that Bodina was a loyal former slave to Urania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Modern historians have created two theories on the origins on the wife of Ptolemy of Mauretania. Urania may have been a mistress from the lower class. Urania was a nickname given to a favorite mistress of a harem. The nickname der
2 CONC ived from the Muses.[5] She was probably a member of the Royal Court in Mauretania.
2 CONT
2 CONT The other theory is that Urania could have been an Assyrian Princess from the Royal family of Emesa. The Royal family of Emesa were a Roman Syrian Client Kingdom and was at the time a leading Kingdom in the Roman East.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Name
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania is an ancient Greek word meaning ‘Heavenly’, ‘Sky’ or ‘Universe’ and is an ancient and modern Greek name. The name Urania is of Emesene origin.[6] Two other Emesene Priest Kings shared the name Uranius, the male variant of 
2 CONC Urania who were Uranius Antoninus who reigned from 210 until 235 and Lucius Julius Aurelius Sulpicius Severus Uranius Antoninus who reigned from 235 until 254. She wasn’t the only Queen to have the name Urania. The Parthian Queen 
2 CONC and wife of Phraates IV of Parthia had the name Thea Urania (Astarte).[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.^ Pir2 I 710
2 CONT  2.^ Ptolemaic Genealogy: Cleopatra Selene
2 CONT  3.^ Cleopatra’s Children and Descendants: credited by Karl Leon Ciccone at Ancient History by Suite101
2 CONT  4.^ Ptolemaic Genealogy: Cleopatra Selene, Footnote 10
2 CONT  5.^ Ptolemaic Genealogy: Cleopatra Selene, Footnote 10
2 CONT  6.^ Ptolemaic Genealogy: Cleopatra Selene, Footnote 10
2 CONT  7.^ Ptolemaic Genealogy: Cleopatra Selene, Footnote 10
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Sources
2 CONT  Royal Egyptian Genealogy, Ptolemaic Dynasty: Cleopatra Selene
2 CONT  Cleopatra’s Children and Descendants at Ancient History by Suite101
2 CONT  E. Groag, A. Stein, L. Petersen - e.a. (edd.), Prosopographia Imperii Romani saeculi I, II et III, Berlin, 1933 - . PIR2 I 710
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Urania
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania [Julia], daughter of Phraates IV, King of Parthia, d35, &, wife, Thea-Urania
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=maclaren&id=I63166
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/discussions/159262 Discussion] on her Unknown Parents: 	
2 CONT Some scattered, easy-to-find references [https://www.geni.com/people/Justin-Swanstr%C3%B6m/6000000007278581048}:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir Anthony Wagner, Pedigree and Progress (1975), Pedigree 19 gives no wife for Ptolemy, king of Mauretania. This book was written before the theory that Julia Urania had any kind of notable ancestry. Wagner sees Drusilla, the 
2 CONC wife of Antonius Felix, as the sister not daughter of Ptolemy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. The Augustan Society’s Descents from Antiquity (1986), Chart P1 comes down to Phaates IV, notes two of his sons, then follows a line down through an unnamed daughter who married Darius of Media Atropatene. No mention of a possi
2 CONC ble daughter Julia Urania. This book was also published before the theory that Julia Urania might have distinguished ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. A biography of Thea Urania Musa, the speculative mother of Julia Urania. Musa was a slave who got the additional names Thea Urania (“Heavenly Urania” = the goddess Astarte) after she bore Phraates IV a son. This biography menti
2 CONC ons her only known child, a son named Phraates V. https://archive.org/stream/AToZOfAncientGreekAndRomanWomenBySamySal...
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. A summary on the prosopography of the royal family of Parthia. Thea Urania Musa is the wife of Phraates IV. She has one known child, Phraates V. Julia Urania is not named at all, either as her child or as one of the children of
2 CONC  Phraates IV by an unknown mother.  http://www.strachan.dk/family/parthia.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. A summary of the prosopography of the Antonii. Iulia Urania is the wife of Ptolemaeus. No further info, no known children.  http://www.strachan.dk/family/antonius.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Will Johnson at soc.genealogy.medieval: “The attribution of Julia Urania as daughter to King Phraates is uncertain. It is mere speculation.”  https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/nmxH...
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Discussion between David Kelley and Marshall Kirk. They support Settipani’s suggestion that Julia Urania was Emesan but think she was wife of Juba II instead of Ptolemy. Part of their argument is that Elagabalus (Roman Emperor 
2 CONC from Emesa 200 years after Julia Urania) used the name Urania for the moon goddess in his sun cult.  http://www.donstonetech.com/SummerInst/EmesaTrevesSeg1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. French Wikipedia: “[Ptolémée de Maurétanie] épouse Julia Urania, dont la tradition fait soit une affranchie gréco-syrienne, soit une membre de la famille royale d' Émèse.”  https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptol%C3%A9m%C3%A9e_de_Ma
2 CONC ur%C3%A9tanie
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. German Wikipedia: (No mention of a wife of Ptolemy II of Mauretania). https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemaeus_(Mauretanien)
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Italian Wikipedia: “Tolomeo sposò Giulia Urania. Urania era una donna sira, probabilmente appartenente alla famiglia reale di Emesa (Homs).”  https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tolomeo_di_Mauretania
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT -------------------- '''
2 CONT =Julia Urania=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Urania (Greek: Ιουλìα Ουρανìа, Latin: Ivlia Urania, flourished 1st century) was a Berber Queen of Mauretania. She married the Berber King Ptolemy of Mauretania, who was a son of the former Mauretanian Monarchs Juba II and Cl
2 CONC eopatra Selene II.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania became Queen of Mauretania, through her marriage to Ptolemy. She married Ptolemy at an unknown date in the 1st century and had borne Ptolemy, a daughter called Drusilla who was born in 38.
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania is only known through a funeral inscription of her Freedwoman Julia Bodina found at Cherchell, Algeria. Cherchell was then known as Caesaria, the capital of the Berber Kingdom of Mauretania in the Roman Empire. In Bodina’s 
2 CONC funeral inscription, Bodina ascribes Urania as Queen Julia Urania. She was ascribed as Queen as a local courtesy or probably a posthumous honor as a dedication to the memory of the former ruling monarch. The inscription reveals th
2 CONC at Bodina was a loyal former slave to Urania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Modern historians have created two theories on the origins on the wife of Ptolemy of Mauretania. Urania may have been a mistress from the lower class. Urania was a nickname given to a favorite mistress of a harem. The nickname der
2 CONC ived from the Muses. She was probably a member of the Royal Court in Mauretania.
2 CONT
2 CONT The other theory is that Urania could have been an Assyrian Princess from the Royal family of Emesa. The Royal family of Emesa were a Roman Syrian Client Kingdom and was at the time a leading Kingdom in the Roman East.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Name'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Urania is an ancient Greek word meaning ‘Heavenly’, ‘Sky’ or ‘Universe’ and is an ancient and modern Greek name. The name Urania is of Emesene origin. Two other Emesene Priest Kings shared the name Uranius, the male variant of Ura
2 CONC nia who were Uranius Antoninus who reigned from 210 until 235 and Lucius Julius Aurelius Sulpicius Severus Uranius Antoninus who reigned from 235 until 254. She wasn’t the only Queen to have the name Urania. The Parthian Queen and
2 CONC  wife of Phraates IV of Parthia had the name Thea Urania (Astarte).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Urania
