1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Mithridates I of Media Atropatene=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Mithridates I of Media Atropatene, sometimes known as Mithridates I and Mithridates of Media (100-66 BC) was a King of Media Atropatene.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Mithridates I was a Median Prince, little is known on his lineage and his life. In or before 67 BC, Mithridates I married an unnamed Armenian Princess from the Artaxiad Dynasty who was a daughter of the Armenian King Tigr
2 CONC anes the Great and his wife, Cleopatra of Pontus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mithridates I ruled from 67 BC to ca. 66 BC. Mithridates I is mentioned in the ancient sources, in the last campaign against the Roman General Lucullus in 67 BC. He was supporting Tigranes, when his father-in-law went to war again
2 CONC st the Romans to invade Cappadocia in 67 BC. There is a possibility that Mithridates I was present with Tigranes the Great and the King Mithridates VI of Pontus, when Tigranes and Mithridates VI were defeated by Lucullus at the Ar
2 CONC sanias River in 66 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mithridates I appeared to have died in ca. 66 BC, as his relative Darius I was King of Media Atropatene in c. 65 BC. According to modern genealogies, Mithridates I and his Armenian wife are presented in being the parents of a chil
2 CONC d, a son called Ariobarzanes I which can explain the claims of Mithridates I’s descendants to the Armenian Kingship in opposition to the lasting ruling monarchs of the Artaxiad Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_I_of_Media_Atropatene
