2 CONT =Sanatruces of Parthia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT King Sanatruces of Parthia (Persian: سیناتروک‎‎) (also Sinatruces or Sanatruk, c. 157-70 BC) ruled the Parthian Empire from ca. 93/2 BC to 88/87 BC during his first reign and ca. 77 to 70 BC during his second reign. He was a membe
2 CONC r of the Arsacid house, who proclaimed himself king in Susiana and attempted to usurp the throne of Mithridates II. Ultimately, Gotarzes I forced him to flee to the Central Asian steppe. Years later, according to work attributed t
2 CONC o Lucian, he regained the throne with the aid of the Sacaraucae Scythians or Saka, an Indo-European tribe akin to the Parthians who had invaded Iran in about 77 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sinatroces, king of Parthia, was restored to his country in his eightieth year by the Sacauracian Scyths, assumed the throne and held it seven years." Makrobioi, 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died c. 70 BC and was succeeded by his son Phraates III.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
