1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Marcus Antonius Felix (Felix in Greek: ο Φηλιξ, born between 5/10-?) was the Roman procurator of Iudaea Province 52-58, in succession to Ventidius Cumanus.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix was the younger brother of the Greek freedman Marcus Antonius Pallas. Pallas served as a secretary of the treasury during the reign of the Emperor Claudius. Felix was a Greek freedman either of Claudius, according to which t
2 CONC heory Josephus (Antiq. xx. 7) calls him Claudius Felix, or for Claudius's mother Antonia Minor, a daughter of Triumvir Mark Antony to Octavia Minor and niece of Emperor Augustus. According to Tacitus, Pallas and Felix descended fr
2 CONC om the Greek Kings of Arcadia.
2 CONT Felix’s cruelty and licentiousness, coupled with his accessibility to bribes (see Book of Acts 24:26), led to a great increase of crime in Judaea. The period of his rule was marked by internal feuds and disturbances, which he put 
2 CONC down with severity. After Paul the Apostle was arrested in Jerusalem and rescued from a plot against his life, the local Roman chiliarch Claudius Lysias transferred him to Caesarea, where he stood trial before Felix. On at least o
2 CONC ne further occasion Felix and his wife Drusilla heard Paul discourse, and later on frequently sent for Paul and talked with him (Acts 24:24-26). When Felix was succeeded as procurator, having already detained Paul for two years, h
2 CONC e left him imprisoned as a favor to the Jews (Acts 24:27). On returning to Rome, Felix was accused of using a dispute between the Jews and Syrians of Caesarea as a pretext to slay and plunder the inhabitants, but through the inter
2 CONC cession of his brother, the freedman Pallas, who had great influence with the Emperor Nero, he escaped unpunished. Porcius Festus succeeded him as procurator of Judea.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriages and issues===
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix married three times. His first wife was princess Drusilla of Mauretania, a maternal second cousin of Emperor Claudius. Drusilla was an only child to Claudius’ late maternal cousin King Ptolemy of Mauretania and his wife Quee
2 CONC n of Mauretania Julia Urania. Claudius arranged for Felix and Drusilla to marry around 53 in Rome. Like Felix, Drusilla was partly of Greek descent. Felix and Drusilla had no children. Felix between 54-56, divorced Drusilla to mar
2 CONC ry another woman.
2 CONT Felix’s second wife was a Judean princess, also named Drusilla, and the daughter of King of Judea Herod Agrippa I, from his wife and cousin Cypros. Felix and the Judean Drusilla, had a son, Marcus Antonius Agrippa, who died along 
2 CONC with this Drusilla and many of the inhabitants of Pompeii and Herculaneum in the eruption of Mount Vesuvius on 24 August 79, and a daughter, Antonia Clementiana. The Judean Drusilla was one of only two major figures reported as dy
2 CONC ing in the eruption of Mount Vesuvius, the other being Pliny the Elder. Antonia Agrippina may have been a daughter from their son's marriage (this name was graffiti in a Royal Tomb in Egypt). Clementiana became a grandmother to a 
2 CONC Lucius Anneius Domitius Proculus. Two possible descendants from this marriage are Marcus Antonius Fronto Salvianus (a quaestor) and his son Marcus Antonius Felix Magnus a high priest in 225. After the eruption, Felix married for a
2 CONC  third time, but little is known about his third wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References===
2 CONT
2 CONT *Tacitus, Annals, xii. 54, Histories v. 9
2 CONT *Suetonius, Claudius, 28
2 CONT *Emil Schürer, History of the Jewish People (1890–1891)
2 CONT *Robertson, A. (1899). "Felix, Antonius". In James Hastings. A Dictionary of the Bible. II. pp. pages 1–2.
2 CONT
2 CONT commentaries on the Acts of the Apostles
2 CONT *Sir W. M. Ramsay, St Paul the Traveller
2 CONT *Carl von Weizsacker, Apostolic Age (Eng. trans., 1894)
2 CONT *Jewish Encyclopedia: FELIX (ANTONIUS FELIX)
2 CONT *http://www.tyndale.cam.ac.uk/Egypt/ptolemies/ptolemies_selene_ii.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonius_Felix
2 CONT
