2 CONT uttermost of your matter. And he commanded a centurion to keep Paul, and to let [him] have liberty, and that he should forbid none of his acquaintance to minister or come unto him. And after certain days, when Felix came with his 
2 CONC wife Drusilla , which was a Jewess, he sent for Paul, and heard him concerning the faith in Christ. And as he reasoned of righteousness, temperance, and judgment to come, Felix trembled, and answered, Go thy way for this time; whe
2 CONC n I have a convenient season, I will call for thee."
