1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Opgalli, a Phrygian noblewoman''',  who may have been a Hellenic Jew - [Tigrane's] wife is only known through numismatic evidence from his kingship. Her royal title is in Greek ΒΑΣ ΟΠΓΑΛΛΥ which means of Queen O
2 CONC pgalli. ΒΑΣ is the royal abbreviation or shortening for the Greek word ΒΑΣΙΛΕΙΑ which means Queen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Opgalli bore Tigranes at least two known children: a son Gaius Julius Alexander and a daughter Julia. Tigranes and his children were the last royal descendants of the Kings of Cappadocia. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tigranes_VI_o
2 CONC f_Armenia
2 CONT
