2 CONT '''Herodes''' (Ἡρῴδης; Hērṓidēs). H. I.; '''Herod the Great'''. Born in c. 73 BC, son of  Antipatter and the Arabian woman Cyprus. In 47 appointed strategos of Galilaea, he came into conflict with the Sanhedrin of Jerusalem becaus
2 CONC e of the execution on his own authority of persons involved in a revolt. The Roman governor of Syria Sex.  Iulius [I] Caesar made him the strategos of Coilesyria and Samaria. 
2 CONT
