1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abgar_V_of_Edessa
2 CONT
2 CONT Abgar V or Abgarus V of Edessa (4 BC - AD 7 and AD 13 - 50) was a historical Syriac ruler of the Syriac kingdom of Osroene, holding his capital at Edessa. According to an ancient legend, he was converted to Christianity by Addai, 
2 CONC one of the Seventy-two Disciples. According to Armenian historian Moses of Khorene he was Sanatruk's relative.
