2 CONT '''Alexandra the Maccabee''' (died ca. 28 BC) was the daughter of '''Hyrcanus II''' (died 30 BC), who was the son of '''Alexander Jannaeus'''.[1] She married her cousin[2] '''Alexander of Judaea''' (died 48 BC), who was the son of
2 CONC  '''Aristobulus II'''. Their grandfather was '''Alexander Jannaeus''', the second eldest son of '''John Hyrcanus'''.[3] Their daughter was the '''Hasmonean Mariamne'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexandra opposed her son-in-law Herod, and when he became sick with grief after having Mariamne executed, Alexandra tried to seize power, but was unsuccessful and was herself executed.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.kittymunson.com/GEDbrows/g1113.html#I22279
