2 CONT
2 CONT The wife of Cnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus, by whom she had a son, who was later to become Nero, Emperor of Rome. After the death of her first husband she became the wife of Claudius, who was at the time Emperor of Rome. She succeede
2 CONC d in having her son adopted by Claudius, and put in line for next emperor, even at the expense of Claudius own son Britannicus. After setting the stage, it is suspected she poisoned Claudius with mushrooms.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Nero became emperor, Agrippina the Younger dominated him completely. However, when Nero adjusted to being Emperor, he had her murdered.(Fuente: Merriam Webster's Biographical Dictionary)
2 CONT
2 CONT She was Aemelia Lepida Minor DI ROMA's (the first of Claudius's wife and my 60th. great grand mother's half-sister.
