2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Nero Julius Caesar=
2 CONT ''' Nero Julius Caesar Germanicus (c. 6-31) was a close relative of the Roman emperors of the Julio-Claudian dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nero was born around AD 6, to Germanicus and Agrippina the Elder. His paternal grandparents were Nero Claudius Drusus and Antonia Minor, daughter of Mark Antony and Octavia Minor. His maternal grandparents were Marcus Vipsanius Ag
2 CONC rippa and Julia the Elder, daughter of Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nero's siblings included four brothers (Tiberius and Gaius Julius, who died young; Drusus Caesar; and the future Emperor Caligula) and three sisters (Agrippina the Younger, Julia Drusilla, and Julia Livilla). In 20, he married Jul
2 CONC ia (daughter of Drusus the Younger), daughter of Livilla and Drusus "Castor" (Tiberius' only son by Vipsania Agrippina). Though earlier he was betrothed to the daughter of Creticus Silanus, one-time governor of Syria.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father Germanicus was heir apparent to his own adoptive father Emperor Tiberius, but Germanicus predeceased the Emperor in 19. He was replaced as heir by Drusus, his father-in-law. But he too predeceased the Emperor on Septemb
2 CONC er 14, 23.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nero was the oldest adoptive grandson of Tiberius, and was seen as the emperor's most obvious successor. However, he was accused of treason along with his mother in 29. Nero was exiled to the island of Ponza where at some time bef
2 CONC ore October 31 he was either induced to commit suicide or else starved to death.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nero_Julius_Caesar
