2 CONT =Drusus Caesar=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Drusus Julius Caesar''', also referred to as '''Drusus III''' (7 – 33), was a member of a noble family of Ancient Rome. He was a son of '''Germanicus''' and '''Agrippina the Elder.''' He was brother to '''Emperor Caligula''', n
2 CONC ephew to Emperor Claudius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus married '''Aemilia Lepida''', daughter of '''Marcus Aemilius Lepidus''', his second cousin. Tacitus reports that during their marriage "she had pursued her husband with ceaseless accusations". In 36, she was charged with ad
2 CONC ultery with a slave and committed suicide, "since there was no question about her guilt" (Tacitus, Annals 6.40).
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus' paternal grandparents were '''Nero Claudius Drusus''' and '''Antonia Minor'''. His maternal grandparents were '''Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa''' and '''Julia the Elder'''. He was ''adopted by his paternal great-uncle'' '''Tibe
2 CONC rius''' after Tiberius' own son, Julius Caesar Drusus, had died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus Caesar was later accused of plotting against Tiberius and was imprisoned in 30, a year after his mother Agrippina the Elder and his brother Nero Caesar were arrested. He starved to death in prison in 33, reduced to chewing 
2 CONC the stuffing of his bed (Annals 6.23).
2 CONT
2 CONT His siblings included two brothers ('''Gaius Julius Caesar (Caligula)''' and '''Nero''') and three sisters ('''Julia Livilla''', '''Julia Drusilla''', and A'''grippina the Younger''').
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------
