1 NOTE Infopedia:
2 CONT Gaius (d. 58 B.C.), general and politician, praetor (61), proconsul of Macedonia (60); m. Atia, niece of Julius Caesar; father of the Emperor Augustus. Marcus (1st century B.C.), general; belonged to Senate party during Civil War;
2 CONC  defeated Dolabella at sea; joined Pompey and fought at Thapsus (46 B.C.) and Actium (31).
