1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Domitius_Ahenobarbus_(consul_16_BC)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus (ca. 49 BC-25 AD) was the son and only child of consul Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus and Aemilia Lepida. His mother was a paternal relative of the triumvir Marcus Aemilius Lepidus. His paternal grandmothe
2 CONC r was Porcia Catonis (sister to Cato the Younger).
2 CONT
2 CONT As a young man Lucius was a renowned and devoted charioteer, perhaps to the point of obsession. He was betrothed in 36 BC, at the meeting of Octavian and Mark Antony at Tarentum, to Antonia Major, the daughter of the latter by Oct
2 CONC avia. He was aedile in 22 BC and consul in 16 BC. After his consulship, he served as governor of Africa from 13/12 BC. He was later probably the successor of Tiberius in Germania, where he commanded the Roman army and crossed the 
2 CONC Elbe, during which he set up an altar to Augustus, and penetrated further into the country than any of his predecessors had done. He also built a walkway, called the pontes longi, over the marshes between the Rhine River and the E
2 CONC ms River. For these achievements he received the insignia of a triumph. He died in 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suetonius described him as "arrogant, cruel, notorious and extravagant," and records numerous instances of his disrespect, to censor Lucius Munatius Plancus, to a proconsul of Africa, to a legate of Illyricum. In his praetorship a
2 CONC nd consulship he brought Roman equites and married women on the stage to perform in pantomimes, which rankled because in Rome acting was considered to be low-class. He exhibited shows of wild beasts in every quarter of the city, a
2 CONC nd his gladiatorial combats were conducted with such excessive bloodshed that Augustus was obliged to put some restraint upon them.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had three children with Antonia Major: Domitia Lepida the Elder, born ca. 8 BC; Domitia Lepida, born ca. 3 BC and mother of the Empress Valeria Messalina; and Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus (cos. AD 32), born ca 1 BC, who was the 
2 CONC biological father of the Emperor Nero.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Domitius_Ahenobarbus_(consul_16_BC)
