1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''שמעון התרסי''' (או שמעון הַתַּסִּי לפי ספר החשמונאים וגם שמעון התטי לפי יוסף בן מתתיהו בספר קדמוניות היהודים; ? - 134 לפנה"ס) היה כהן גדול ונשיא היהודים החל משנת 143 לפנה"ס. הוא היה בן לשושלת החשמונאים, בנו השני
2 CONC  של מתתיהו הכהן.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simon_Thassi '''Simon Thassi'''] (died 135 BCE) was the second son of Mattathias and thus a member of the Hasmonean family. The name "Thassi" has an uncertain meaning ("the Director", "the Guide", "th
2 CONC e Man of Counsel", and "the Zealous" are all possible meanings of the term)
2 CONT
2 CONT He took part in the Jewish revolt against the Seleucid Empire led by his brothers, Judas Maccabaeus and Jonathan Maccabaeus. He became the first prince of the Hebrew Hasmonean Dynasty. He reigned from 142 to 135 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hasmonean Dynasty was founded by a resolution, adopted in 141 BCE, at a large assembly "of the priests and the people and of the elders of the land, to the effect that Simon should be their leader and high priest forever, unti
2 CONC l there should arise a faithful prophet" (1 Maccabees xiv. 41).
2 CONT
2 CONT Recognition of the new dynasty by the Roman Republic was accorded by the Senate about 139 BCE, when the delegation of Simon was in Rome. Simon made the Jewish people semi-independent of the Seleucid Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT In February 135 BCE, he was assassinated at the instigation of his son-in-law Ptolemy, son of Abubus. Simon was followed by his third son, John Hyrcanus, whose two elder brothers, Mattathias and Judah, had been murdered, together 
2 CONC with their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%A9%D7%9E%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%9F_%D7%94%D7%AA%D7%A8%D7%A1%D7%99  '''שמעון התרסי]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jdp-fam&id=I64694  '''Simon Thassi''' rootsweb]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Simon III (Thassi) Hasmonean   Birth:	estimated between 260BCE and 200BCE Immediate Family:	 Husband of Rabbi Yossel ben Yohanan  Father of Yohanan (John) I Hyrcanus  Added by:	Gerene Mae JENSEN on August 23, 2015 Managed by:	Gere
2 CONC ne Mae Mason (Jensen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mihály László FARKAS (08-10-2015):  I disconnected from his "male spouse"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Simon Thassi=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Maccabeus (also referred to as Simon Thassi, Hebrew: שמעון התרסי; died 135 BC) was the second son of Mattathias and thus a member of the Hasmonean family. The name "Thassi" has an uncertain meaning ("the Director", "the Guid
2 CONC e", "the Man of Counsel", and "the Zealous" are all possible meanings of the term)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He took a prominent part in the Jewish revolt against the Seleucid Empire led by his brothers, Judas Maccabaeus and Jonathan Maccabaeus. The successes of the Jews rendered it expedient for the pretenders to the throne of Syria to 
2 CONC show them special favor, and therefore Antiochus VI. appointed Simon strategus, or military commander, of the coast region from the Ladder of Tyre to Egypt. As strategus Simon conquered the cities of Beth-zur and Joppa, garrisonin
2 CONC g them with Jewish troops, and built the fortress of Adida in the plain.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the capture of Jonathan, Simon was elected leader by the people, assembled at Jerusalem; he at once completed the fortification of the capital, and made Joppa secure by expelling its Gentile inhabitants and filling it with J
2 CONC ews (I Macc. xiii. 8, 10, 11; "Ant." xiii. 6, § 4). At Hadid he blocked the advance of the treacherous Trypho, who was attempting to enter the country and seize the throne of Syria. Since Trypho could gain nothing by force, he dem
2 CONC anded a ransom for Jonathan and the surrender of Jonathan's sons as hostages. Although Simon was fully aware that Trypho would deceive him, he acceded to both demands, so that the people might see that he had done everything possi
2 CONC ble for his brother. Jonathan was nevertheless treacherously assassinated, and the hostages were not returned. Simon thus became the sole leader of the people.
2 CONT
2 CONT As the opponent of Trypho, Simon had every reason to side with Demetrius II., to whom he sent a deputation requesting freedom from taxation for the country. The fact that his request was granted implied the recognition of the poli
2 CONC tical independence of Judea.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became the first prince of the Hebrew Hasmonean Dynasty. He reigned from 142 to 135 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hasmonean Dynasty was founded by a resolution, adopted in 141 BCE, at a large assembly "of the priests and the people and of the elders of the land, to the effect that Simon should be their leader and high priest forever, unti
2 CONC l there should arise a faithful prophet"
2 CONT
2 CONT Recognition of the new dynasty by the Roman Republic was accorded by the Senate about 139 BCE, when the delegation of Simon was in Rome. Simon made the Jewish people semi-independent of the Seleucid Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT In February 135 BC, he was assassinated at the instigation of his son-in-law and rival Ptolemy, son of Abubus. Simon was followed by his third son, John Hyrcanus, whose two elder brothers, Mattathias and Judah, had been murdered, 
2 CONC together with their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simon_Thassi
