1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gaius Julius Caesar (proconsul)=
2 CONT Gaius Julius Caesar jr (ca. 130-85 BC) was a Roman senator, supporter and brother-in-law of Gaius Marius, and father of Gaius Julius Caesar, the later dictator of Rome - [[6000000001336610897]].
2 CONT
2 CONT Caesar was married to Aurelia Cotta, a member of the Aurelii and Rutilii families, and had two daughters, both named Julia as was common in Rome, and a son, Julius Caesar, born in 100 BC. He was the brother of Sextus Julius Caesar
2 CONC  (consul in 91 BC) and the son of Gaius Julius Caesar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caesar's progress through the cursus honorum is well known, although the specific dates associated with his offices are controversial. According to two elogia erected in Rome long after his death, Caesar was a commissioner in the 
2 CONC colony at Cercina, military tribune, quaestor, praetor, and proconsul of Asia. The dates of these offices are unclear. The colony is probably one of Marius' of 103 BC. Broughton dated the praetorship to 92 BC, with the quaestorshi
2 CONC p falling towards the beginning of the 90s. Brennan has dated the praetorship to the beginning of the decade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caesar died suddenly in 85 BC, in Rome, while putting on his shoes one morning. Another Caesar, possibly his father, had died similarly in Pisa. His father had seen to his education by ''one of the best orators of Rome, Marcus Ant
2 CONC onius Gnipho.'' In his will, he left Caesar the bulk of his estate, but after Marius's faction had been defeated in the civil war of the 80s BC, this inheritance was confiscated by the dictator Sulla.
2 CONT ====Reference: ====
2 CONT [https://bit.ly/2Im0WhE Wikipedia - Gaius Julius Caesar (proconsul)]<br/>
2 CONT ''(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaius_Julius_Caesar_(proconsul))''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Caius Julius Caesar III, the Praetor (died 0084 BC)===
2 CONT He was a Praetor (93/92 BCE), and Proconsul Asiae (91 BCE). Gens Iulia was originally composed of several different families, including Asinius, Bassus, Caesar, Libo and Mento. By this generation, however, the Caesars were apparen
2 CONC tly the only surviving family among the Iulii.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died : 84 BC 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Family==== 
2 CONT '''Father:''' Caius Julius Caesar II<br/>
2 CONT '''Mother:''' Marcia - daughter of Quintus Marcius Rex<br/>
2 CONT '''Siblings:''' Julia<br/>
2 CONT '''Spouse:''' Aurelia<br/>
2 CONT ====Children:====
2 CONT # '''Julia Caesar''' died 0051 BC Julia died at an early age
2 CONT # '''Caius Julius Caesar IV ("the Julius Caesar")''' born 12 July 0100 BC died March 0044 BC<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT =====[[6000000014835656244]] was his 15th great grandfather.=====
