2 CONT =Manius Aemilius Lepidus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Manius Aemilius Lepidus was the son of Marcus Aemilius Lepidus the Younger and consul of Rome in 11 AD. Tacitus reports that Augustus on his deathbed, while discussing possible rivals for the Roman Emperor Tiberius, described him 
2 CONC as worthy of becoming emperor (capax imperii), but "disdainful" of supreme power.
2 CONT
2 CONT He defended his sister Aemilia Lepida at her trial in 20 AD. He had a daughter also called Aemilia Lepida.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 21 AD, Tiberius appointed him to the governorship of Asia.
2 CONT
