1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sextus Cocceius Vibianus
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sextus Cocceius Vibianus was a Roman Senator in 204. He was the son of Sextus Cocceius Severianus and grandson of Sextus Cocceius Severianus, Proconsul and Legate of Africa between 161 and 163, and wife Caesonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married and had a daughter, who married Quintus Anicius Faustus Paulinus (born ca 180), Legate of Moesia Inferior between 229 and 230 or c. 230 to 232, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Sources
2 CONT  Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989).
2 CONT  Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines, A L'Epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite. Linacre, UK: Prosopographica et Genealogica, 2000. ILL. NYPL ASY (Rome) 03-983.
2 CONT  Anthony Wagner, Pedigree and Progress, Essays in the Genealogical Interpretation of History, London, Philmore, 1975. Rutgers Alex CS4.W33
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sextus_Cocceius_Vibianus
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Sextus Cocceius Vibianus=
2 CONT '''
