2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aspacures_III_of_Iberia Aspacures III of Iberia, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Aspacures III (or Varaz-Bakur II, Georgian: ვარაზ-ბაკურ II), of the Chosroid Dynasty, was the king of Iberia (Kartli, eastern Georgia) from c. 380 to 394. He was the son and successor of Mirdat III and was married to the daughter 
2 CONC of Trdat, his relative and successor. He is credited by the Georgian chronicles with the construction of the church of Tsilkani.[1] During his reign, the Roman Empire signed the Peace of Acilisene with Sassanid Iran in which it ad
2 CONC mitted to the loss of Iberia and a greater portion of Armenia. His sons were Pharasmanes and Mihrdat.
2 CONT
