2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Aspacures III (or Varaz-Bakur II) Georgian and Daughter of Trdat 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mihrdat_IV_of_Iberia Mihrdat IV  of Iberia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mihrdat IV (Georgian: მირდატ IV, Latinized as Mithridates), of the Chosroid Dynasty, was the king of Iberia (Kartli, eastern Georgia) from c. 409 to 411.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Varaz-Bakur II and the grandson (on his mother’s side) of Trdat. The Georgian chronicles criticizes him for impiety and neglect of religious building, and informs us that he opposed both major regional powers, th
2 CONC e Roman and Sassanid empires.[1] Defeated by the Sassanid army, he was captured and deported to Iran, where he died.
2 CONT
