1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In Greek mythology,.......
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleodaeus was one of the Heracleidae, a grandson of Heracles. He was the son of Heracles's eldest son [https://www.geni.com/people/Hyllus/6000000002187622536 Hyllus] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Iole/6000000002187622545 Iole o
2 CONC f Oechalia]. He became father of Aristomachus, who led the third attempt to capture Mycenae and failed. He also had a daughter Lanassa, who married Neoptolemus and had by him several children, including Pyrrhus. Cleodaeus had a he
2 CONC roon at Sparta.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleodaeus
