2 CONC 57OPDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=Quintus+Caecilius+Metellus+Pius+Scipio&pg=PA112&printsec=frontcover]
2 CONT “Quintus Caecilius METELLUS Pius SCIPIO Nasica
2 CONT A tribune in 59, Metellus was born into the Cornelii Scipiones family and adopted into th Caecilii Metelli family—an illustrious lineage unequaled in Rome. He and cato were bitter enemies, in part because Metellus married Aemilia 
2 CONC Lepida, whom Cato had intended to marry. He was prosecuted by Favonius in 60 [BC], he also detested Caesar, although he remained friend with Pompey. He became Pompey’s consular colleague in 52 [BC]after Pompey married his daughter
2 CONC  Cornelia. He committed suicide in North Africa after defeat at the hands of Caesar in the civil war in 46 [BC].”
