2 CONT =Tiberius Gracchus the Elder=
2 CONT '''Tiberius Gracchus major''' (maior, Latin for the elder - to distinguish him from his eldest son, the famous tribune; Latin: TI·SEMPRONIVS·P·F·TI·N·GRACCVS) (ca. 217 BC – 154 BC) or '''Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus''' was a Roman
2 CONC  politician of the 2nd century BC. '''Tiberius''' was of Plebs or plebeian status and was a member of the well connected gens Sempronia, family of ancient Rome. '''Tiberius''' was the son of '''Publius Sempronius Gracchus''', appa
2 CONC rently the younger brother of the two-times consul and general '''Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus''' (killed 212 BC). His paternal grandfather was also a consul in 238 BC. His mother's identity is not known.
2 CONT *His father was ''not the same'' '''''Publius Sempronius Gracchus''''' ''who served as tribune of the plebs in 189 BC'', and the father had possibly died during the Second Punic War, since no further references exist to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Tiberius's family=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tiberius''' married the eighteen-years-old '''Cornelia Africana''' in 172 BC when he was about 45 years, thus considerably her senior. Despite the age difference, the marriage was happy and fruitful. She bore him ''twelve child
2 CONC ren'', but all of them were sickly and most of them died in infancy despite their parents' assiduous care. 
2 CONT *Three children survived to adulthood; 
2 CONT # a daughter '''Sempronia Gracchae''' (who was betrothed to her mother's first cousin '''Scipio Aemilianus'''), and two sons, 
2 CONT # the Roman politicians '''Tiberius Gracchus''' and 
2 CONT #'''Gaius Gracchus'''.
2 CONT
