1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucius Julius Caesar (c. 134 – 87 BC) was a Roman statesman and general of the late second and early first century BC. He was elected Praetor of Rome in 94 BC. In 93 BC, as Propraetor, he was governor of Macedonia.
2 CONC  In 90 BC he was made elected the highest office of Cousul of the Roman Republic.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Caesar and his brother, Gaius Julius Caesar Strabo Vopiscus, were killed in 87 BC during the Civil War between Gaius Marius and Lucius Cornelius Sulla.[13] After Sulla had left for the East to fight against Mithridates of P
2 CONC ontus, Marius returned from banishment and started executing his political opponents.[14] Lucius and Gaius were among his first victims.[13] According to Livy, their heads were displayed on pikes on the speaker's platform (the Ros
2 CONC tra) in the Forum.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children, by his wife Fulvia,[15] were Lucius Julius Caesar, who was consul in 64 BC, and Julia, who would later become the mother of Mark Antony.
