2 CONT Barzabod was a high-ranking Iranian official in 5th-century Sasanian Iran. A Mihranid prince of the Gardman region,[1] he served as the viceroy of Caucasian Albania.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Georgian chronicler Juansher, Barzabod married off her daughter Sagdukht to his Iberian neighbor, Mihrdat V, then heir apparent to King Archil of Iberia, and eventually king in his own right. The marriage helped t
2 CONC o seal peace between the once hostile neighbors. After Archil's death c. 435, Sagdukht relied on her father for support during her regency for her underage son, Vakhtang I of Iberia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barzabod died around 440, and was succeeded by his son Varaz-Bakur.
