2 CONT Bakur II ( _ka. ბაკურ II, Latinized as "Bacurius"), of the Chosroid Dynasty, was a king of Iberia (natively known as Kartli; ancient Georgia) from 534 to 547 A.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bakur was the son and successor of King Dachi. According to the medieval Georgian chronicler Juansher, he died leaving young children and Iberia fell under the Sassanid control. [Martindale, John Robert (1992), "The Prosopography 
2 CONC of the Later Roman Empire", p. 169. Cambridge University Press, ISBN 0521072336.]
2 CONT
