2 CONT Sources: Ancestral Roots 45; Kraentzler 1669, 1680, 1795. K-1795: Constantius I, Emperor of Britain, Gaul, Spain and Rome ("Chlorus"). His British name appears to have been Cystennan. K-1669: Flavius Constantius "Chlore," Emperor 
2 CONC of Britain, Rome and Gaul. Roots: Theodora Comnena, married Constantinus Angelus.
2 CONT
2 CONT =========================
2 CONT
2 CONT Constantinos was the governor of Dalmatia, and appointed Caesar to rule Gaul and Britain March 1, 293. Born in Illyria 214, he was trained in the hard school of warfare on the Danube frontier. Constantius I became Emperor of Rome 
2 CONC in May 305, and in right of his wife, King of England. He was born in 242 and died at Eboracum (present day York, England) on July 25, 306. The son of Helen and Constantius I was Constantine the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT =================
2 CONT
2 CONT file:///E:/E-S009/genealogy/Grab_A_Site_downloads/stirnet/romans2.htm#link4
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Constantius Chlorus, Emperor of Rome (b 242, d 07.306) m1. (div) Helena 'of the Cross' (d 328, possibly dau of Coilus, King of Cochester) ... m2. Theodora (dau of Maximianus Herculius, Emperor of Rome) @4@ above ...
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Constantius I (Flavius Valerius Constantius Chlorus) "the Pale", Emperor of Rome
2 CONT
2 CONT Governor of Dalmatia, appointed Caesar to rule Gaul and Britain March 1, 293. He was the son of *Eutropious, a Dardanian nobleman descended from the *Gordiani, and his wife, *Claudia, daughter of *Claudius II (Marcus Aurelius Flav
2 CONC ius Claudius Gothicus), a virtuous and worthy Roman Emperor (268-270), who was a soldier, statesman, and a distinguished officer. Born in Illyria 214, he was trained in the hard school of warfare on the Danube frontier, and died o
2 CONC f the Plague in 270, aged 55, whereupon his brother Marcus Aurelius Claudius Quintillus became Emperor. Constantius I became Emperor of Rome in May 305, and in right of his wife, King of England. He was born in 242 and died at Ebo
2 CONC racum (present day York, England) on July 25, 306. On becoming "Caesar," he was required by Diocletian to put aside *Helena and to take Maximian's stepdaughter, Theodora, as his wife. From the first union, *Helena and *Constantius
2 CONC  I had an illegitimate son, *Constantine the Great. He married (2) Theodora, daughter of Maximinus, Roman Emperor. Gibbon says *Claudia was the niece of *Claudius II (Marcus Aurelius Flavius Claudius Gothicus). Encyclopedia Britta
2 CONC nica maintains Constantius I's descent from Claudius Gothicus was a fiction.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: "Neuman-Smith-Goodale Family and Ancestors" Michael R. Neuman michaelneuman@earthlink.net (who has generously shared the above narrative at AWTP.)
