1 NOTE KNOWN AS "CLORUS"; AN ILLYRIAN; ROMAN EMPORER (CAESAR 293, AUGUSTUS 305)
1 NOTE His full name is Flavius Valerius Constantius, called Constantius Chlorus. 
2 CONT  He was a general and administrator under Emperor Maximian, who adopted 
2 CONT him and gave him the government of Gaul and the rank of caesar in 293. 
2 CONT When his coemperors, Maximian and Diocletian, abdicated in 305, 
2 CONT Constantius became emperor in the West and prepared to conquer the Picts 
2 CONT of Scotland. He died during the campaign, after proclaiming his son 
2 CONT Constantine his successor as emperor.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
