2 CONT Constans' birthdate is calculated by counting backwards from his age at the time of his death. Sources indicate that he died at either 27 or 30 (DiMaio, Zonaras , 281, n.16; Jones, Martindale, and Morris, PLRE , 1.220). This would
2 CONC  place his birth at some date between 320 and 323, although Barnes, relying on numismatic evidence, argues for the year 323 ( New Empire , 45). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2The surviving books of Ammianus Marcellinus' history begin with events in the Fall of 353. Cross-references in his extant books to earlier lost books suggest that he gave significant coverage to Constans. See further, R. Frakes, 
2 CONC "Cross-References to the Lost Books of Ammianus Marcellinus," Phoenix 49 (1995): 232-246, esp. 243-45. 
