2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''19th Sassanid King of Iran'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kavadh_I
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Interreigne de Balash (Valkash)
2 CONT
2 CONT In that period, the Persian king Kawad sent his son to a Manichaen school in their  country where he learned their doctrine and pledged to his teachers that if he should  come to rule he would uphold their heresy. [The Manichaean 
2 CONC teachers] said: "We will  pray that you reign." Now the boy's mother urged Kawad to enthrone her son during his  own lifetime. The king understood the reason for this and was frightened that other kings  [in future] would heed [th
2 CONC e Manichaeans] and that people would say that it was during  his rule that Magianism had been destroyed. And so [Kawad] convened a great assembly  and invited to it all the Manichaeans with their bishops and destroyed them. As for
2 CONC  those  discovered outside, he had them burned alive, and gave their churches to the Christians.  This became known in Constantinople where there were also many Manichaeans. And  an attempt was [g234] made — unsuccessfully — to tu
2 CONC rn them away from their heresy.  They too, generally were burned to death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sukhra was in charge of government of the kingdom and the management of affairs. The people came to Sukhra and undertook all their dealings with him, treating Kavadh as a person of no importance and regarding his commands with co
2 CONC ntempt"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kavadh_I (sassanid, persia). Sejarah Melayu mentions him as "raja masyrik dan maghrib" which means "east and west". Also called Kobat Shahriar, Kobad Shah, Qobad.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kavadh_I
