0 @N6000000002187597423@ NOTE Osroene
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT (Redirected from Osrhoene)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Osroene (also: Osrohene, Osrhoene; Syriac: ?????? ???? ???? ?????), also known by the name of its capital city, Edessa (modern Sanli Urfa, in Syriac: ?????), was one of several kingdoms arising from the dissolution of the Seleucid
1 CONC  Empire. The Syriac kingdom occupied an area on what is now the border between Syria and Turkey.
1 CONT
1 CONT It was in this region that the "legend of Abgar" originated, for which see Abgarus of Edessa.
1 CONT
1 CONT Osroene was absorbed into the Roman Empire in 114 as a semi-autonomous vassal state, then incorporated as a province in 214.
