1 CONT
1 CONT Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa (c. 63 BC–12 BC) was a Roman statesman and general. He was a close friend, son-in-law, lieutenant and minister to Octavian, the future emperor Caesar Augustus. He was responsible for most of Octavian’s mil
1 CONC itary triumphs, most notably winning the naval Battle of Actium against the forces of Mark Antony and Cleopatra VII of Egypt.
1 CONT
1 CONT Contents [hide]
1 CONT 1 Early life 
1 CONT 2 Rise in power 
1 CONT 3 Life in public service 
1 CONT 4 Late life 
